<title>RUSSIA: Moscow international airport charges in April.</title>
<headline>Moscow international airport charges in April.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Federal Aviation Service has approved new price schedules for Moscow airports.</p>
<p>Below are charges, in roubles, for April, including landing fees per tonne of maximum take off weight (L), maintenance fees on an hourly basis (M), per international passenger charges (P) and international cargo and mail charges per kg (C).</p>
<p>Charges do not include value added tax.</p>
<p>Fuel charges per tonne (F) and charges for meteorological (W) data have not been released:</p>
<p>			L	 M	    P	 C     F     W</p>
<p>    Sheremetyevo  40,560  123,519  30,240    690   n/a   n/a</p>
<p>    Domodedovo    38,550  110,000  30,000    825   n/a   n/a</p>
<p>    Vnukovo	 47,400  113,800  42,370  1,020   n/a   n/a</p>
<p>    Plane	  Weight in tonnes  Plane	Weight in tonnes</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-62	161.6	Antonov An-124    392.0</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-62M     167.0	Antonov An-225    600.0</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-96-300  224.4	Antonov An-32	27.0</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-86	210.0	Antonov An-30	22.7</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-76T/TD  190.0	Antonov An-28	 6.5</p>
<p>    Ilyushin Il-76MF    210.0	Antonov An-26	24.0</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-154M     100.0	Antonov An-24	21.8</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-154B	98.0	Antonov An-12	61.0</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-204	 94.6	Yakovlev Yak-40    16.1</p>
<p>    Tupolev Tu-134	 47.6	Yakovlev Yak-42    54.0</p>
<p>--Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
